00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.389 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  i've always loved teachers but with all  the additional challenges they're facing  right now  i can say without a doubt they are real  life superheroes and i mean capes and  all  and in honor of national teacher day i  get the pleasure of talking to an  amazing special education teacher  from the bronx everybody let's say hello  to jamel  holmes  thank you thank you okay you're from  east  bronx academy for the future correct all  right will you  talk about this school sure um i'm a  sixth grade teacher  and you know i get really excited about  talking about east bronx academy  specifically because i was a student  there and graduated in 2008  and i came back 10 years later in 2018  to become a special education teacher  there  you go above and beyond for your  students will you please tell us about  that  sure so i've done tons and tons of  things for my students but one of the  things that i really really love to talk  about  is the trip that we do to the barber  shop because  this really sets the tone and teaches  our children outside of the classroom  ways in which to be presentable having a  male role model  and also offer mentorship so every  year we go to the barber shop and my  barbie  does free haircuts for us and the  students are so so excited  and they're like am i really getting a  haircut today like i'm at the barber  shop with my teacher  have you ever read the book crown by  derek barnes  no i haven't oh my god it's so beautiful  it's this children's book  and it's about this boy going to a  barber shop and it's  poetic and artistic and beautifully  illustrated  by gordon james and they're actually  friends of the show so i'm going to get  you and your students this book because  it really speaks to that moment what do  you think the goal  of a teacher should be so specifically  my goal as a teacher is to really build  these relationships with students  beyond the classroom i really just want  to be  that role model that the students have  they can come to me  and have these conversations about  whatever's happened in their lives  many of our students come from unstable  houses and one parent single-parent  houses and things like that  so i want to be that person that they  can kind of go to beyond the school  there was a moment where my daughter  olive was missing a school assignment  online and we were scrambling  and she was actually going to her dad's  for the weekend  and we were just it was the height of  corona you know  the pandemic and we were trying to  figure out the transitions and we always  talk about you know how transitions are  hard  and i was like oh god and you're late  for your online class and i just  put my head in my head and i said you  know what olive right now  i want to talk about there's school  smart and there's life smart  and we're working on life smart so the  lesson can wait  because i know this school you're going  to be school smart  but right now we're working on life  smart we talk about school and it's so  big and global  and we're trying to reform education  right now but school supplies is  something that really speaks to you  yes definitely school supplies so a  specific experience is throughout the  pandemic  i was able to purchase food  school supplies everything my students  need so i went out  and i drove up to students houses and  they came downstairs and  and students kind of got those things  that they need and those are kind of the  relationships that i love to have  with my students well we have a special  delivery actually mr postman jim  are you here special delivery for  jamelle it's a big bag  um there is an amazing company called  school specialty  and they wanted to donate to you this  entire bag is filled with school  supplies  thank you so much i cannot wait to share  this with my students  we are just so in awe of everything you  do  and your students are as well in fact  jim  i believe there's another special  delivery perfect  she'll deliver some mail thank you jim  so much thank you jamal you actually  have a little homework tonight yourself  these are letters that your students  have written to you  thank you wow and i'm sure that  everybody just wants to sky right and  shout off the rooftops  that everything you're doing is what we  need to know about  and shine a light on and you're just so  awesome and thank you  you're the living example of what is  possible from and from a teacher  and it's more than what's in the  classroom i believe that with all my  heart i didn't even go to school  and i love life smart but i'm so  passionate about education and my girls  i want them to be in school for the next  50 years  but it is about real life as well as  what happens in that classroom  and you are just straddling that line  with such grace and beauty and i  am in awe of you and i thank you so much  for coming on this show thank you so  much phil  i love to be here and i wouldn't be  anywhere else today  than right here talking about the  amazing work that's happened in the  bronx  and the stuff that i'm doing my students  well we also just have to say before we  go to commercial that you are giving a  head  to toe look jamal really thank you  you are bringing it you're amazing  [Music]  you

